**user**:
> In Shiny, within a mainPanel, how do I put two sliderTextInputs next to each other?
**assistant**:
> To place two `sliderTextInput` elements next to each other in a `mainPanel` in Shiny, you can use the `fluidRow` and `column` functions to manage the layout. By assigning each `sliderTextInput` a specific width using the grid system (out of a total of 12 columns), you can align them horizontally. Here is an example of how you can structure your UI:
> 
> ```r
> library(shiny)
> library(shinyWidgets)
> 
> ui <- fluidPage(
>   mainPanel(
>     fluidRow(
>       column(6,
>              sliderTextInput(
>                inputId = "slider1",
>                label = "Slider 1",
>                choices = c("A", "B", "C"),
>                selected = "A"
>              )
>       ),
>       column(6,
>              sliderTextInput(
>                inputId = "slider2",
>                label = "Slider 2",
>                choices = c("D", "E", "F"),
>                selected = "D"
>              )
>       )
>     )
>   )
> )
> 
> server <- function(input, output, session) {}
> 
> shinyApp(ui, server)
> ```
> 
> In this example, each `sliderTextInput` is placed inside a `column` function with a width of 6, resulting in a total width of 12 columns for the fluid row, which aligns the sliders side-by-side. Adjust the column sizes as needed to fit your specific layout preferences.
